{"id": null, "total_replies": 2, "hidden_replies": 0, "replies": [{"id": 238, "parent": null, "created": 1626624495.2753308, "modified": null, "mode": 1, "text": "<p>I just bought this book because of your review!</p>", "author": "Akiyama", "website": null, "likes": 1, "dislikes": 0, "notification": null, "hash": "21ab34aaf0fa", "total_replies": 0, "hidden_replies": 0, "replies": []}, {"id": 268, "parent": null, "created": 1644698018.17172, "modified": null, "mode": 1, "text": "<blockquote>\n<p>things like big-game hunting and metalworking are always male tasks, and things like spinning, dairying, and primary child care are &quot;women's work.&quot;</p>\n</blockquote>\n<p>The <a href=\"https://cdn.substack.com/image/fetch/f_auto,q_auto:good,fl_progressive:steep/https%3A%2F%2Fbucketeer-e05bbc84-baa3-437e-9518-adb32be77984.s3.amazonaws.com%2Fpublic%2Fimages%2F7c101d17-3777-46e5-83d6-c230bbe97dfd_768x1196.png\" rel=\"nofollow noopener\">actual table</a> from Murdock and Provost 1973 (reproduced in <a href=\"https://naturalselections.substack.com/p/competition1of2\" rel=\"nofollow noopener\">Heather Heying's post on Competition</a>) is enlightening.</p>", "author": "Zack M. Davis", "website": "http://unremediatedgender.space/", "likes": 1, "dislikes": 1, "notification": null, "hash": "5d7d0749de49", "total_replies": 0, "hidden_replies": 0, "replies": []}], "config": {"reply-to-self": true, "require-email": true, "require-author": true, "reply-notifications": false, "gravatar": false, "feed": true}}